course: dictionary
lesson: 9690
title: Suffocate: when there is not enough air
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Suffocate means you cannot breathe because there is not enough air. A person or animal that suffocates can become very ill or even die. Read the words around it: in «Never let anyone climb into a washing machine, tumble dryer or old fridge; children can be trapped and suffocate, which means they cannot breathe», the clue is "which means they cannot breathe".
explain: Suffocate can also mean stopping something from getting air. In the marsh, «roots can suffocate» means the roots cannot get the air they need. To check, swap in your meaning: "children can be trapped and cannot breathe" still makes sense, so you have understood it.
explain: You may also hear suffocating or feel suffocated. Here it is a feeling, not a real lack of air: it means trapped, held back, or very hot and stuffy. Ask yourself: is someone really unable to breathe, or do they only feel that way?
fact: Suffocate is a verb: suffocate, suffocates, suffocated, suffocating.
fact: «Suffocate» means to be unable to breathe because there is not enough air.
fact: To suffocate something means to stop it getting air.
fact: «Suffocating heat» means heat so strong that it feels stuffy and hard to breathe in.
fact: Plastic bags are not toys, because they can cover the nose and mouth and suffocate a child.
exercise: «Never let anyone climb into a washing machine, tumble dryer or old fridge.» What does suffocate mean in this safety rule? | To be very happy and full of song | *To be unable to breathe because there is not enough air | To fall asleep quickly | To be painted bright red
exercise: Fire needs oxygen, so a fire blanket suffocates flames. What does suffocates mean here? | Lights the flames again | Paints the flames a new colour | Makes the flames grow taller | *Stops the flames getting the air they need
exercise: Find and copy the word in «roots can suffocate and dead plants hardly rot» that means the roots cannot get the air they need. | dead | rot | roots | *suffocate
test: Jo says, «I feel suffocated in this crowded room.» What does she mean? | She cannot breathe at all and needs a doctor | She is very tall | *She feels trapped, hot and stuffy | She is painted with water
test: Why must children never be shut in a fridge or car? | Because the car door is too heavy | Because fridges are only for food | Because the fridge would be too loud | *Because they could suffocate, as there is not enough air
exam: Which meaning fits best in «a plastic bag can suffocate a child»? | A child is painted bright blue | A child runs very fast | A child loses the bag in the park | *A child cannot breathe because there is not enough air
